 "subjects": ["ANY",{"id":"FENCE","exclude":true},{"id":"POOL_BARRIER","exclude":true}],
 "conditions": [[{"fact":"development_footprint_exists","op":"IS_FALSE"},{"fact":"boundary_type","op":"IN","value":["SIDE","REAR"]}]],
 "sources": [{"key":"lsc_seaspray_res_side_rear","role":"PRIMARY","quote":"AO5.2 Buildings or structures (other than fences) have a setback from side and rear lot boundaries in accordance with the following: ... (b) where located in the Seaspray Residential Low Density Precinct or the Seaspray Residential Medium Density Precinct and the lot does not have an approved building location envelope: (i) a setback of at least 1.5 metres;"}],
 "interpretation_notes": "No Class 10a concession and no low-structure or rainwater-tank exemption in AO5.2 (only fences are excluded); retaining walls and pools are literally caught. Pool barriers treated as fences. No approved building location envelope (BLE) read as development_footprint_exists = false; where a BLE exists the development must be within it (not encoded). Fences excluded by the text. The local plan code prevails over zone codes (s1.5(d)), so these rules OVERRIDE every zone-based LSC.C setback rule; the underlying zone of the Seaspray area was not confirmed by the research, which this makes immaterial.",
 "effective_from": "2025-05-02"}$r$);
